PRAYER

In the light of the matters stated in the above Replication, the Plaintiff most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:

a) Reject the Written Statement and the preliminary objections raised by the Defendant as being untenable in law and on facts;

b) Reject the counter-claim filed by the Defendant, if any, with exemplary costs;

c) Decree the suit in terms of the prayer clause of the Plaint dated ____;

d) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the interest of justice.

And for this act of kindness, the Plaintiff shall ever pray.
